The landing page (site/relate/1.0.1/ and site/relate/1.3.0/) serves, unmodified, files from the npm package
@relate/relate-wasm versions 1.0.1 and 1.3.0 (relate.js, relate_bg.wasm, trap.js, snippets/, package.json),
Relate compiled to WebAssembly, published under the Apache License 2.0 (https://github.com/relatedb/relate).
Their source tarballs, registry integrity hashes and per-file SHA-256 are listed in site/relate/engines.json;
scripts/vendor_relate_wasm.py fetches and verifies them, and its --verify mode downloads the pinned tarballs again and
compares every served file with them, byte for byte. The tarballs carry no licence file of their own, so the text of
the Apache License 2.0 is served beside the engines as site/relate/LICENSE.txt.
